Bump package version 0.0.11 → 0.1.0 and promote the `## [Unreleased]`
CHANGELOG content into a dated `## [0.1.0] - 2026-07-02` section (fresh empty
`## [Unreleased]` added above it), using Keep-a-Changelog categories.

The 0.1.0 release covers the Beads→Kernel default switch plus the three PRs
merged for this release:

- #270 (Fixed): `forge export` now actually projects Kernel issues to
  git-tracked JSONL (dispatcher broker injection + `jsonl` outbox target) — the
  Kernel git-persistence/portability loop works end to end.
- #269 (Changed): pre-merge is an embedded doc gate inside `/ship` and
  `/review`, not a numbered stage or an invokable `/premerge` command.
- #271 (Changed): packaging — exclude a stray test from the npm tarball, add
  `engines.node >=22.16.0`, document `forge doc-gate`.

No version-hardcoded tests needed updating: `forge --version` reads the version
dynamically from package.json, and the only `0.0.11` literal in tests
(release.test.js) is a deliberate negative test asserting an unsupported
release-readiness target — it correctly stays as-is.

Verified: `forge release check --json` → success:true, target 0.1.0, 0 blockers;
`forge --version` → v0.1.0; release + docs-consistency tests green (32/0);
`eslint . --max-warnings 0` clean.

